      <h1><a href="/boolean-thinking/">The case against boolean logic</a></h1>

      <div class="entry">
        <p>In my last post about generality, I tried to show how our ambition to discover ideas that are all-encompassing and eternal makes our worldview crumble, leaving us unable to think clearly even about simple issues with obvious solutions. Today, I want to discuss another instance of the same problem, in a simpler and more direct way. You can think of this essay as a prequel to “<a href="/universal-knowledge/">When Universality Breaks</a>.”</p>


